3. YOUR PROJECT AND CODE

SchutzelDev can suggest changes to files within the directory from which it is run
and its subdirectories.

Before a suggested code change is written, SchutzelDev displays the proposed changes
and asks for your approval. Changes generated by the local language model are
restricted to the directory in which SchutzelDev is run and its subdirectories.

You should run SchutzelDev from the root directory of the project you want to work on.

You are responsible for reviewing proposed changes before accepting them. You should
maintain appropriate backups and, where appropriate, use version control for your
projects.

SchutzelDev uses a local language model. Like any AI-assisted software, it may produce
incorrect, incomplete, or unsuitable results. You are responsible for reviewing and
validating its output before relying on it.


